The United States Wrestling Association is a professional wrestling organization that operates out of Tennessee. Formed by the merging of the Texas based World Class promotion and the Memphis based CWA, the USWA ran shows in both territories for a brief period, including television deals in both Memphis and Dallas. Eventually the Texas portion failed and the USWA became a Memphis only promotion, led by Jerry Jarrett and built around long time Memphis legend Jerry "The King" Lawler.
